        22,
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/mona_iowa",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Mona was named by Caine after his Isle of Man sweetheart, Ramona Johnson.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        6,
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/mona_iowa",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Mona Lutheran Church, organized in 1876, still stands in its 1882 building.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
